Project Legends License Overview
================================

Project Legends is a multi-component repository. It is not distributed under a
single MIT license. This file is an overview of the licenses and license
markers currently present in the repository; it does not relicense any file.

Where a source file has an SPDX-License-Identifier, that identifier is the
file-level license marker. Where third-party code carries its own license text
or notice, that text controls that component. See `COPYING` for the GNU General
Public License version 2 text and `NOTICE` for third-party attribution.

The GPL-2.0-only versus GPL-2.0-or-later question is not resolved here. Some
project documentation currently uses GPL-2.0-only language, while many current
Project Legends source files use `SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later`.
This overview records those facts only; the owner decision is reserved for the
separate licensing cleanup work.

Component license table
-----------------------

| Path | Current license markers / notices | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `engine/` | GPL, from the vendored DOSBox-X fork and related engine code. `NOTICE` identifies DOSBox-X as GNU GPL v2.0; `COPYING` contains GPL v2 text. | Includes the vendored DOSBox-X-derived engine and local engine bridge code. This row does not decide GPL-only versus or-later beyond the current notices. |
| `src/legends/`, `src/app/`, `src/pal/`, `src/engine_host/`, `src/main.cpp` | Current source SPDX tags observed in these trees are `GPL-2.0-or-later`. | These components link to or participate in the GPL engine path. |
| `include/legends/`, `include/pal/` | Current source SPDX tags observed in these trees are `GPL-2.0-or-later`. | Public headers for the GPL-linked embedding and PAL surfaces. |
| `src/legends_ipc/`, `include/legends_ipc/` | Current source SPDX tags are `MIT`. | IPC protocol and serialization code intended to remain independent of GPL engine objects. |
| `src/legends_proxy/` | Current source SPDX tags are `MIT`. | IPC proxy surface intended to link only MIT IPC code. |
| `external/glad/` | Current source SPDX tags are `GPL-2.0-or-later`. | Repository-local GL loader files as currently tagged. |
| `external/stb/` | `stb_truetype.h` states public domain. `stb_image_write.h` offers MIT License or public domain. | Third-party stb single-header components retain their embedded notices. |
| `tests/` | Mixed current SPDX tags: mostly `GPL-2.0-or-later`, with IPC/proxy/isolation tests and helpers tagged `MIT`. | Test files follow their file-level SPDX markers. |
| `benchmarks/` | Mixed current SPDX tags: `GPL-2.0-or-later` and `MIT`. | Benchmark files follow their file-level SPDX markers. |
| `scripts/` | Mixed current SPDX tags: `GPL-2.0-or-later` and `MIT`. | Script files follow their file-level SPDX markers. |
| `cmake/` and root CMake files | Current tagged template file uses `GPL-2.0-or-later`; root `CMakeLists.txt` says GNU GPL v2.0 in comments. | Build metadata does not create a new license grant. |
| `.github/`, `.githooks/` | Workflow comments currently say GNU GPL v2.0 where marked; other automation files may be unmarked. | CI and repository automation follow their explicit notices where present. |
| `docs/`, `spec/`, `openspec/` | Documentation/specification files are a mix of unmarked project documentation and explicit component statements; `openspec/changes/phase-iso-process-isolation/specs/wire-format/spec.md` references an MIT SPDX requirement for the wire format. | Existing documentation statements are descriptive and may not match current source SPDX tags. |
| `DEPENDENCIES.md` and CMake FetchContent dependencies | Dependency manifest lists gsl-lite (MIT), SDL3 (Zlib), GoogleTest (BSD-3-Clause), Google Benchmark (Apache-2.0), SDL2 (Zlib), FluidSynth (LGPL-2.1), MUNT/mt32emu (LGPL-2.1), and zlib (Zlib). | `NOTICE` contains third-party attribution. CMake fetches pinned dependency versions when they are not installed locally. |
| `COPYING` | GNU General Public License version 2 text. | License text, not a source component. |
| `NOTICE` | Third-party attribution and license summary. | Attribution file; no source headers changed by this overview. |
| `AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `AUDIT.md`, `AUDIT_REPORT.md`, `CIFix.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `README.md`, `REFACTORING_CHANGELOG.md`, `RELEASING.md`, `REQUIREMENTS.md`, `TLA_CONFORMANCE.md`, `tlaAudit.md` | Top-level project documentation; some files describe GPL/MIT component boundaries and some are unmarked. | This overview does not add a separate license grant for documentation beyond existing notices. |
| `CHANGELOG.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `roadmap.md`, `TODO.md` | Top-level project planning/release notes; unmarked in this pass. | Not modified by this Sprint 0 license overview. |
| `CMakePresets.json`, `requirements-dev.txt`, `.gitattributes`, `.gitignore`, `.codex/`, `.claude/`, `audit-wiki/`, `graphify-out/`, `build_log.txt`, `build_output.txt` | Repository metadata, generated/audit output, or local tooling records; no separate source license marker was added here. | These entries are listed so top-level repository contents are not hidden by the old single-license file. |

External dependency attribution
-------------------------------

The root `NOTICE` file identifies the third-party projects incorporated by or
used by Project Legends. The current dependency manifest is `DEPENDENCIES.md`;
the pinned versions used by CMake are in `cmake/dependencies.cmake`.

No source SPDX headers were added, removed, or changed as part of this
overview.
